  "notes": "Geometric for «لكن الله يشهد» and «عليما حكيما», a book for «بما أنزل إليك», stars for the heavens. No motif on the angels, the Messenger or the Fire (167-169 under a night sky). 166:7-8 «أنزله بعلمه» not glossed (As-Sa'di gives two readings). STAGING v4: 166 stays ambient: Allah's and the angels' testimony for the Prophet. 167-169: a small group (3) of disbelievers in a town at dusk shakes their heads on 167:3, turns their backs on 167:5 (rejecting and turning away from the way of Allah) and walks off on 167:10 (far astray); they stay on stage during 168-169 and nothing falls on them; two-paths plate on 168:12, ending before the Name on 169:10; Hell is not drawn. 170: the address to all people: a mixed group in a market, camera only; nothing is acted on the command 170:9 or the conditional 170:12-13; nothing stands for the Messenger; light plate for the truth, stars for the heavens, geometric for the closing names."
